Assuming you have MR, the blast damage will be 2d10 points, or 11
points on average.  Also, if I read the source right, the blast damage
occurs before the invocation effect, meaning that a successful
invocation of the staff will heal half of it (assuming the blast
didn't kill you, of course).

Thus, successfully invoking the staff ought to give you a net HP gain
on average if you're more than 11 points below your maxHP, and will
always do so if you're more than 20 points below maxHP (again assuming
that the blast won't kill you, which can happen if you only have 20 HP
or less left).  For combat classes with relatively high maxHP, this
should leave a rather wide margin.

As for the staff's value as a melee weapon, maxing your luck ought to
give you pretty much 100% hit rate even at basic, and the double
damage against non-drain-resistant monsters is nothing to sneer at.
That said, it probably does lose to stormy + silver saber in Gehennom,
since all demons are drain-resistant.

